    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jonathan Aranda** stands out as our premier offensive anchor. With a score of 65.57, he benefits significantly from a favorable 4.55 xERA matchup against Lugo and a prime spot batting second in the order. His high xwOBA of 0.375, combined with a 12% boost from a beneficial platoon split, positions him to lead our production. **Bryson Stott** (62.84) also provides strong value, as his profile gains traction from a neutral-to-hitter-friendly park environment against Cavalli, while **Lawrence Butler** (60.31) and **Cal Raleigh** (60.29) round out our high-efficiency core. The decision to place **Cal Raleigh** in the two-hole is a calculated risk; while the dynamic platoon split against the right-handed Chandler is a slight deterrent (-6%), his elite placement in the batting order (+8%) outweighs the matchup volatility.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved evaluating **Jung Hoo Lee** (49.23) against the remaining depth. While his score is respectable, he ultimately fell into the marginal category because of a -10% platoon penalty against Springs. We are prioritizing our higher-floor starters given the game cap constraints. We must remain vigilant regarding the status of **Geraldo Perdomo**, whose game is currently marked as a rainout, ensuring he is fully removed from all considerations. With **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** remaining on the IL and **Yainer Diaz** and **Tyler Freeman** unavailable due to lineup rotations and off-days, our bench depth is intentionally thin today to preserve our remaining season caps for high-leverage opportunities involving players like **Masyn Winn**, **Luis Arraez**, or **Daulton Varsho**. No additional wind or park warnings were triggered, so the priority remains minimizing exposure to elite arms\u2014thankfully, none of our active starters are facing an xERA below 3.90 today.",
